  "latest_findings": {
    "dual_battery_result": "Two packs are admitted as an energy-management architecture, not as an energy source. One pack may support only the Axle torque deficit/startup/transients while the second preserves regenerative headroom and collects verified AFPM/PEMFC surplus; roles may swap under BMS supervision.",
    "authoritative_energy_metric": "For any battery-neutral claim use E_A + E_B. Swapping or charging one pack from the other does not count as generation.",
    "support_battery_nuance": "The support pack need not be the primary source of rotation. As hydraulic/process torque rises, its motor contribution can fall toward zero; above the motor/regen crossover the AFPM can charge the recovery pack from independently sourced shaft work.",
    "power_electronics_boundary": "Prefer controlled bidirectional DC/DC stages and BMS/contactors rather than direct battery-to-battery alternation, to avoid uncontrolled equalization currents and preserve clean energy accounting.",
    "regen_headroom": "A second pack can deliberately remain below full SOC, preventing genuine regenerative pulses from being discarded because the support pack is already full."
  },
